---
import CodeBlock from "../../components/ui/CodeBlock.astro";
import ModelSection from "../../components/models/ModelSection.astro";
import ModelLayout from "../../layouts/ModelLayout.astro";
import { sectionLookup } from "../../lib/models";

const sections = [
  {
    id: "comparison",
    title: "Comparison with Jev",
  },
  {
    id: "model-at-a-glance",
    title: "Model at a glance",
  },
  {
    id: "quickstart",
    title: "Quickstart with Nouli CLI",
  },
  {
    id: "provenance",
    title: "Base models and training data",
  },
  {
    id: "limitations",
    title: "Limitations",
  },
  {
    id: "license-and-citation",
    title: "License and citation",
  },
];
const section = sectionLookup(sections);
---

<ModelLayout slug="nouli-doom" sections={sections}>
  <Fragment slot="intro">
    <p>
      Nouli Doom is a PPO-trained policy for ViZDoom Deadly Corridor at skill 5. The inference
      export contains the actor network and maps structured game state to move, strafe, turn, and
      fire decisions.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
  <ModelSection {...section("comparison")}>
    <p>Recorded comparison with Jev 1.14.0, dated 31 October 2026.</p>
    <p>
      <video
        controls
        muted
        playsinline
        preload="metadata"
        poster="/models/nouli-doom/comparison.png"
        aria-label="Nouli Doom and Jev recorded side-by-side simulator episode"
      >
        <source src="/models/nouli-doom/comparison.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
        <a href="/models/nouli-doom/comparison.mp4">Open the recording</a>
      </video>
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/models/nouli-doom/comparison.mp4">Open the side-by-side recording</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Collect the green armor and finish alive in Deadly Corridor. <strong>Nouli Doom</strong> and
      the recorded <strong>Jev</strong> setup start from the same game state with the same
      structured-state and goal interface.
    </p>
    <p>
      In this recorded episode, Nouli collects the armor and survives; Jev's run ends before
      collecting it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Playback follows simulator time; a panel holds its last available frame when its recording
      ends. This example was selected after scoring and illustrates this recorded setup, not a
      general ranking of the models.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-doom/resolve/v1.0.0/eval/results.json">
        Recorded evaluation
      </a>{" "}
      ·{" "}
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-doom/resolve/v1.0.0/eval/protocol.json">
        Setup and limitations
      </a>
      .
    </p>
  </ModelSection>
  <ModelSection {...section("model-at-a-glance")}>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Property</th>
          <th>Value</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Parameters</td>
          <td>23,435</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Input</td>
          <td>42-float structured state; 54 legal joint actions</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Tested runtime</td>
          <td>macOS and Linux ARM64 / CPU</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>License</td>
          <td>Apache-2.0; upstream notices apply</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </ModelSection>
  <ModelSection {...section("quickstart")}>
    <p>
      Requires Python 3.12, the{" "}
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/docs/huggingface_hub/guides/cli">HF CLI</a>, and{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/nouli-ai/nouli/releases/tag/v0.4.2">Nouli CLI 0.4.2</a>. Hugging
      Face hosts the files; inference runs on your machine. The Python server loads the weights, and
      Nouli runs the supplied decision workflow. No hosted API key is required.
    </p>
    <p>In the first terminal:</p>
    <CodeBlock
      label="Terminal 1 · prepare and serve"
      code={`hf download nouli-ai/nouli-doom --revision v1.0.0 --local-dir ./nouli-doom
cd nouli-doom
python3.12 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
python prepare.py --input-json examples/input.json
python serve.py --device cpu
`}
    />
    <p>
      Once the server reports ready, open a second terminal in <code>nouli-doom</code>:
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      label="Terminal 2 · run the workflow"
      code={`nouli --config nouli/nouli.toml --store ./.nouli-store \\
  workflow run nouli/example-workflow.json --json
`}
    />
    <p>
      This example returns one action for the supplied state. Running an episode also requires the
      simulator loop to apply actions and provide each next state.
    </p>
  </ModelSection>
  <ModelSection {...section("provenance")}>
    <ul>
      <li>Student: a PPO multilayer perceptron.</li>
      <li>
        Teacher:{" "}
        <a href="https://huggingface.co/fabiononato/doomfly-rl/tree/2e58329dcdeed64107679f0ff113b024d4d2b167">
          <code>fabiononato/doomfly-rl</code>
        </a>
        , checkpoint <code>malecns49k_noconn</code>.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>Training data: Teacher trajectories, DAgger and simulator reinforcement learning.</p>
    <p>
      Trained through imitation learning from the public Doomfly teacher and simulator reinforcement
      learning. Doomfly supplied labels; its weights are not the student's direct initialization.{" "}
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-doom/resolve/v1.0.0/provenance.json">
        Source revisions and provenance
      </a>
      .
    </p>
  </ModelSection>
  <ModelSection {...section("limitations")}>
    <ul>
      <li>Validated on Deadly Corridor at skill 5 with the supplied state/action wrapper.</li>
      <li>
        Inputs include structured state and goal assistance; these results do not establish
        pixel-only or general Doom performance.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </ModelSection>
  <ModelSection {...section("license-and-citation")}>
    <p>Apache-2.0, with upstream notices and dataset attribution retained.</p>
    <p>
      <a href="https://nouli.ai">Nouli AI</a>. Nouli Doom. Cite the published model version and
      commit.
    </p>
  </ModelSection>
</ModelLayout>
